{"id":"word:hebrew:H7931","type":"word","title":"שָׁכַן","subtitle":"H7931 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"to reside or permanently stay (literally or figuratively)","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to שָׁכַן (H7931) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: v.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 129 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"שָׁכַן (shâkan) means to reside or permanently stay (literally or figuratively) First listed occurrence: 1Chr 17 9."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"שָׁכַן","transliteration":"shâkan","pronunciation":"shaw-kan'","strong":"H7931","lemmaId":"hebrew:H7931","partOfSpeech":"v","forms":["יִשְׁכְּנוּ","לְ/שַׁכֵּ֥ן","יִשְׁכֹּ֥ן","שֹׁכֵ֖ן","שֹׁכֵ֥ן"],"morphs":[["HVqi3ms",17],["HVqi3mp",11],["HVqrmsa",10],["HR/Vpc",8],["HR/Vqc",7],["HVqi3fs",7],["HC/Vqq1cs",6],["HC/Vqw3ms",5],["HVqp3ms",5],["HC/Vqq3ms",4]]},"definitions":{"short":"to reside or permanently stay (literally or figuratively)","usage":"abide, continue, (cause to, make to) dwell(-er), have habitation, inhabit, lay, place, (cause to) remain, rest, set (up).","full":"H7931. shakan or shaken שָׁכֵ֑ן שָׁכַן, verb settle down, abide, dwell (Late Hebrew id. ; Ecclus 43:17d +; Phoenician שכן Lzb 375 ; Aramaic שְׁכֵין ; Syriac , all dwell ; Arabic rest, dwell , compare Assyrian šakânu, set , lay , deposit , set up (a dwelling), intransitive be situated (of city), maškanu, place, dwelling-place ); — Qal Perfect 3masculine singular ׳שׁ Exod 40:35 5 t.; שָׁכֵ֑ן Deut 33:12 2 t., etc.; Imperfect 3masculine singular יִשְׁכֹּן Gen 16:12 +; יִשְׁכָּןֿ Num 9:17 2 t.; 3 masculine plural יִשְׁכֹּ֑נוּ Jer 49:31 ; 3 feminine plural תִּשְׁכֹּ֑נָּה Ezek 17:23 , etc.; Imperative masculine singular שְׁכֹן Gen 26:2 ; Psa 37:27 ; שְׁכָןֿ 37:3 ; masculine plural שִׁכְנוּ . Jer 48:28 ; Infinitive construct בִּשְׁכֹּן (Ges § 45g ) Gen 35:22 , לִשְׁמֹּן 2Chr 6:1 , etc.; suffix שָׁכְּנִי Exod 29:46 ; שִׁכְנוֺ Deut 12:5 (but see Pi`el 1 ), etc.; Participle שֹׁכֵן Gen 14:13 +, שֹׁכְּנִי (Ges § 90 l m ) Deut 33:16 3 t.; suffix feminine singular שֹׁכַנְתְּי Jer 51:13 ; Passive participle , apparently plural construct with art, הַשְּׁכוּנֵי Judg 8:11 (but corrupt, proper name, of a location needed, see GFM): — 1 settle down to abide : a. of person: encamp Num 24:2 (E); settle permanently Psalm 102:29 (absolute: || יִכּוֺן ); ׳שׁ כמלך Job 29:25 (|| ישׁב ); settle down (to remain) Judg 5:17 ; תַּחְתָּיו 2Sam 7:10 = 1Chr 17:9 (not to be removed); especially at rest, peace, in security, לבטח Jer 23:6 ; 33:16 ; Deut 33:12 , compare כתפים בין 33:12 ; Psa 16:9 ( ןן שׂמח ); בטח Deut 33:28 ; Prov 1:33 ; (ל)בדד Num 23:9 (poem) Jer 49:31 ; Micah 7:14 ; land of Egypt Jer 46:26 (remain undisturbed), so 50:39 ; Isa 13:20 (|| תֵּשֵׁב , compare ישׁב 4 ); with מרומים Isa 33:16 ; absolute Nahum 3:18 , subject אדּירים (We רָֽשְׁנוּ , Now יִשְׁכְּבוּ ; || נָמוּ ); Prov 7:11 her feet tarry not in her house . b. of animals: כְּלָבִיא Deut 33:20 ; ב location Isa 34:11 ; Job 37:8 ; שָׁם Isa 13:21 ; birds ׳שׁ תַּחַת (under) Ezek 17:23 , ׳שׁ בְּצֵל 17:23 ; with עַל = upon 31:13 , = by Psa 104:12 ; with accusative סֶלַע Job 39:28 ; absolute, of man under figure of bird, וְאֶשְׁכֹּ֑נָה אָע֫וּפָה Psa 55:7 . c. things: with עַל of cloud, Job 3:5 settle down over ; compare Exod 24:16 ; 40:35 ; Num 9:17-18 , 22 (all P); with בְּ 10:12 (P). 2 abide, dwell : a. of men: absolute Psa 37:27 ( לְעוֺלָם ); שָׁ֫מָּה Isa 65:9 ; with ב location Psalm 69:37; Job 18:15 ; 30:6 ; Micah 4:10 ; Jer 48:28 10 t.; יִמִּים לְחוֺף Gen 49:13 ; with עַל , by Judg 5:17 ; Jer 51:13 ; upon Jeremiah 37:29; פני על Gen 16:12 (J); with עִם with Psa 120:5 ; 120:6 ; with accusative Prov 2:21 ; Jer 17:5 5 t.; עַד ֗֗֗ מִן Gen 25:18 (J); אָ֑רֶץ שֹׁכְנֵי Isa 18:3 (|| תֵבֵל ישְׁבֵי ). b. of the dead: עָפָר שֹׁכְנֵי Isa 26:19 (|| רְפָאִים ); compare Job 26:5 (|| id. ), so mortals; חֹמֶר בָתֵּי שֹׁכְנֵי 4:19 ; ׳שׁ דוּמָה Psa 94:17 (i.e. שׁאול ). c. of God: ׳שׁ בָּֽעֲרָפֶל 1Kin 8:12 2Chr 6:1 (poem); מָרוֺם Isa 33:5 ; עַד 57:15 ; וְקָדוֺשׁ מָרוֺם 57:15 ; ׳שׁ סְנֶה Deut 33:16 (theoph.); בְּאָֽהֳלֵישֵֿׁם Gen 9:27 (J, see Br MP 82 ; al. Japheth subject); בְּתוֺכָם Exod 25:8 ; 29:46 ; Num 5:3 (all P), Ezek 43:9 ; with בְּתוֺךְ elsewhere Exod 29:45 (P) + 6 t.; ב location Psa 85:10 ; later בְּצִיּוֺן Joel 4:17; Joel 4:21; צִיּוֺן בְּהַר Isa 8:18 ; Psa 68:17 ; 68:19 (absolute) + 4 t.; יְרוּשָׁלִַם שֹׁכֵן 135:21 . d. things: מוֺעֵד אֹהֶל , with את Lev 16:16 (P); י ׳מִשְׁכַּן שָׁם Josh 22:19 (P); אוֺר Job 38:19 . e. abstract subj,: מִשְׁמָּט Isa 32:16 ( בַּמִּדְבָּר ); חָכְמָה with accusative עָרְמָה Prov 8:12 . Pi`el Perfect 3masculine singular שִׁכֵּן Psa 78:60 ; 1 singular שִׁכַּנְתִּי Jer 7:7 , 12 ; Imperfect 1singular אֲשַׁכְּנָה 7:3 ; Infinitive construct שַׁכֵּן Num 14:30 7 t.; suffix שַׁכְּנוֺ Deut 12:5 (so read for לְשִׁכְנוֺ ᵑ0 , compare Kö ii. l. 21 ); — 1 make settle down, establish: שׁ ׳אֹהֶל בָּֽאָדָֽם Psa 78:60 especially in Deuteronomy, שָׁם שְׁמוֺ לְשַׁכֵּן establish his name there (compare šakan šuma as Canaanism Wkl TelAm.138 Rev. 20; 181.6 ) Deut 12:11 ; 14:23 ; 16:2 , 6 , 11 ; 26:2 , compare Jer 7:12 ; Neh 1:9 ; + לְשִׁכְנוֺ שָׁם אֶתִשְֿׁמוֺ לָשׂוּם Deut 12:5 (read לְשַׁכְּנוֺ ). 2 make to dwell : with accusative of person, ב location, Num 14:30 (J) Jer 7:3 , 7 . Hiph`il Perfect 1singular הִשְׁכַּ֫נְתִּי Ezek 3:24 ; Imperfect 3masculine singular jussive יַשְׁכֵּן Psa 7:6 , וַיַּשְׁכֵּן Gen 3:24 ; Psa 78:55 , etc.; &#8212; 1. a. lay , לעפר כבודי lay my honour in the dust (of death); place, set , Gen 3:24 (J); place, establish , מועד אהל at Shilo Josh 18:1 (P). b. cause birds to settle , עַל Ezek 32:4 . 2 cause to dwell , with accusative of person, ב location, Psa 78:55 ; compare Job 11:14 .","rootNote":"a primitive root (apparently akin (by transmission) to 7901 through the idea of lodging; compare 5531 , 7925 );","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 17 9","keyReferences":["1Chr 17 9",